@startuml
!include ./nora-medlink-style.puml
title Figure 3.7 — Nora MedLink Sequence Diagram: Appointment Booking

actor Patient
participant "Next.js Appointment Page" as Frontend
participant "FastAPI Appointment API" as API
participant "Auth Dependency" as Auth
participant "Doctor Directory Query" as Directory
participant "Dashboard Access Service" as Access
database "PostgreSQL Database" as DB

Patient -> Frontend : Search doctor and select slot
Frontend -> API : GET /appointments/doctors
API -> Directory : Query registered and demo doctors
Directory -> DB : Read doctor users and profiles
DB --> Directory : Doctor rows
Directory --> API : Filtered doctors
API --> Frontend : Doctor list
Patient -> Frontend : Confirm appointment details
Frontend -> API : POST /appointments
API -> Auth : require_patient(token)
Auth --> API : Authenticated patient
API -> DB : Resolve selected doctor
DB --> API : Doctor or demo doctor result
API -> DB : Insert Appointment(status=BOOKED, payment=PENDING)
opt Patient provides dashboard access OTP
  API -> Access : grantTemporaryDashboardAccessByOtp()
  Access -> DB : Validate OTP and upsert access row
  DB --> Access : Access status
  Access --> API : Access granted flag
end
DB --> API : Appointment saved
API --> Frontend : Booking response
Frontend --> Patient : Show appointment confirmation
@enduml
